# StudyBuddy demo disk guard — install to /etc/cron.d/studybuddy-disk-check
#
# Hourly at :17. Offset from the backups (02:00 daily, 03:00 Sunday) and from
# the top of the hour, where everything else on this box already piles up.
#
# Hourly rather than daily because the failure mode is not gradual: on
# 2026-08-31 the box went from working to 100% full and took the demo down at
# the next deploy, and a daily check would have left up to 24 hours in which the
# only symptom was a failed deploy nobody was watching for.
#
# The script is quiet when healthy, prunes caches on its own above 70%, and only
# emails above 80% / 90% — at most one mail per level per day. So this line is
# not a source of routine noise; if it mails, something needs a person.
#
# Output appends to /var/log/studybuddy-disk.log, alongside the backup log, so
# the history is there when Promtail is eventually switched on (it is installed
# but inactive on this box today — which is why the alert is an email and not a
# log query).
SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin

17 * * * *  root  cd /opt/studybuddy && bash scripts/demo/disk-check.sh >> /var/log/studybuddy-disk.log 2>&1
